  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n[Respond to base URL changes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#respond-to-base-url-changes) iterates over _descendant_, but the inner steps use _element_, which isn't defined there:\n\n> For each _descendant_ of _document_'s shadow-including descendants:\n>\n> 1. If _descendant_ is a `script` element whose result is a speculation rules parse result:\n>\n>     1. Let _oldResult_ be _element_'s result.\n>     2. Let _newResult_ be the result of creating a speculation rules parse result given _element_'s child text content and _element_'s node document.\n>     3. Update speculation rules given _element_'s relevant global object, _oldResult_, and _newResult_.\n\nI think _element_ should be _descendant_.\n",
